  "tuning": {
   "seeds": "0-11",
   "grid": "gust mean {0,2,3,4,5,6} x R_min {3,4.5} at pace 3.0 (and pace 3.5 earlier)",
   "target": "40-70% bot completion",
   "chosen": "gust mean 3.0, R_min 3.0: 50% on the tuning seeds"
  },
  "why": [
   "The wing swarm's edge in v1 was raw speed (5.5 studs/s vs 1.5 to 1.9 for the beetles). A moving squall caps progress at its pace, so speed alone no longer wins: running ahead is outside the disc too.",
   "Keeping 15 bots inside a shrinking disc through 3-stud tunnels and a 6-stud shore strip forces the formation to stretch into a column and regroup, which is what the swarm work (quorum, formation) is about.",
   "The gust shore turns the old reef bay into the hazard: with the reef gone there is nowhere to stand, and the crosswind punishes bots on the water-side lane, so formation placement matters.",
   "Each part has one knob (pace, final radius, gust mean), so the course can be tuned to a target completion rate."
  ]
 },
